## What is and is not established

Established for H1: the suspect upper-right arc is depicted by a continuous
solid outline. Local roughness, interior hatch spaces, and separate grid
losses explain the visual discontinuity concern without supplying evidence
for an intentional dashed arc.

Not established: the physical production stage responsible for particular
ragged or missing grid pixels (printing, scanning, or later processing).
Calling them reproduction/ink losses here is a visual description, not a
forensic attribution. No claim is made that every missing pixel in the full
source has the same cause.

No label is newly transcribed. No radius, cutoff, intercept, other panel,
whole-page source fact, modern figure, or answer is re-reviewed. This local
resolution does not silently resolve any other held/unreadable fact.

